Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 20:16:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] Phase 4 firmware: epcs_remote_reconfig + mode 'r' +
 mode 'g' tail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the user-facing firmware glue for the now-functional
wb_altremote_update wrapper (see prior commit for the RTL fixes
that made S_RECONFIG actually reachable).

New compilation unit remote_update.{h,c}:
- epcs_remote_reconfig(pgm_sel) (noreturn): drain UART TX FIFO,
  write 29-bit payload to wrapper DATA reg (PGM_SEL[23:0]=pgm_sel,
  WD_EN=0, AP_CONFIG_SEL=0), trigger SHIFT_IN_AND_RECONFIG.
- 29-bit shift-register layout documented per Cyclone IV Handbook
  Vol 1 Ch 8.

main.c integration:
- New mode 'r' (standalone, no SD card needed): print mode banner +
  trigger line, call epcs_remote_reconfig(0) to boot factory ALINX
  from EPCS page 0.
- mode_generate (Phase 8) tail now calls epcs_remote_reconfig(0)
  instead of halting — closes the loop on the altremote pipeline
  end-to-end.  Multi-slot rotation deferred to Phase 9.
- Dispatcher menu updated: r=reconfig.

Stage2 ELF: 17148 → 17424 B (+276 B for the new function + strings).
IMEM 32 KB has plenty of headroom (54% used).

Silicon-verified on bitstream md5 60094abc — UART capture
diag_phase4_nh12_reconfig_ok.log shows stage2 boot → dispatcher → 'r'
trigger → factory ALINX banner appearing on the wire.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
